~ Abstract

<!-- TODO Rewrite -->
Effect systems are a programming language feature that has gained in popularity recently.
However, most implementations still incur significant performance overhead for stack operations.
Tracing JITs are an approach to just-in-time compilation that uses dynamic execution traces.
On microbenchmarks,
we show that, by leveraging the existing RPython toolkit for generating tracing jits to implement a bytecode interpreter,
many stack operations are optimized away.
This causes significant speedups, also when comparing to a backend compiling directly to machine code ahead-of-time via LLVM.
~

