|:~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~:|~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| _(const)_   | $< memory // x <- v; stmt >$                                | $-->$ | $< memory\{x \mapsto v\} // stmt >$             |                                      |
| _(prim)_    | $< memory // \many{x_i} <- primitive f(\many{x_j}); stmt >$ | $-->$ | $< memory\{\many{x_i\mapsto v_i}\} // stmt>$    | if $f(\many{memory(x_j)}) = \many{v_i}$ |
| _(evi here)_ | $< memory // x <- here; stmt > $ | $-->$ | $< memory\{x \mapsto here\} // stmt >$ | | <!-- = CONST_INT, but may be nicer to have this here, too? -->
| _(evi there)_ | $< memory // x <- there; stmt > $ | $-->$ | $< memory\{x \mapsto there\} // stmt >$ | | <!-- = CONST_INT, but may be nicer to have this here, too? -->
| _(evi add)_ | $< memory // x_1 <- x_2 \oplus x_3; stmt >$                      | $-->$ | $< memory\{x_1 \mapsto v\} // stmt >$           | if $v = memory(x_2) \oplus memory(x_3)$         | <!-- Alternatively, drop this and treat as primitive? -->

_Register Management_

<!-- Maybe even drop this from the calculus? This does not add much and is quite natural for an actual bytecode implementation -->

|:~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~:|~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| _(copy)_    | $< memory // x_1 <- x_2; stmt >$                            | $-->$ | $< memory\{x_1 \mapsto v\} // stmt >$                     | if $v = memory(x_2)$                    |
| _(swap)_    | $< memory // x_1 \leftrightarrow x_2; stmt >$               | $-->$ | $< memory\{x_1 \mapsto v_1, x_2 \mapsto v_2\} // stmt >$  | if $v_1 = memory(x_1), v_2 = memory(x_2)$  |
| _(drop)_    | $< memory // drop x; stmt >$                                | $-->$ | $< memory\vert_{dom(memory)- x} // stmt >$                    | if $v = memory(x_2)$                    |

_Data and codata_

|:~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~:|~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| _(new)_    | $< memory // x <- new V(\many{x_j}); stmt >$  | $-->$ | $< memory\{x \mapsto <V,\many{v_j}>\} // stmt >$ | if $v_j = memory(x_j)$    |
| _(invoke)_ | $< memory // x.m(\many{x_i}) >$  | $-->$ | $< \{\many{x_k \mapsto v_k}\} // stmt' >$ | if $\many{v_k} = \many{memory(x_i)}, \many{v_j}$ |
|            | | |                                                                            | and $\{ l(\many{x_k}): stmt' \} = V(m)$ |
|            | | |                                                                            | and $memory(x) = <V,\many{v_j}>$ |
| _(cons)_   | $< memory // x <- tag(\many{x_i}); stmt >$ | $-->$ | $< memory\{x \mapsto <tag,\many{v_i}>\} // stmt >$ | if $v_i = memory(x_i)$ |
| _(match)_  | $< memory // x match \{ \many{tag_c(\many{x_{ic}}) => B_c} \} >$ | $-->$ | $< memory\{\many{x_{ic} \mapsto v_i}\} // jump B_c >$ | if $tag_c = tag$ and $memory(x) = <tag,\many{v_i}>$

_Jumps_

|:~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~:|~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| _(jump)_      | $< memory // jump \{label(\many{x_j}): stmt\} >$                       | $-->$ | $< memory\vert_{\many{x_j}} // stmt >$                     |           |
| _(if t)_      | $< memory // if x_1 then \{label(\many{x_i'}): stmt_1\}(\many{x_i}) else stmt_2 >$ | $-->$ | $< \{\many{x_i' \mapsto v_i}\} // stmt_1 >$ | if $v_i = memory(x_i)$ |
| | | | | and $memory(x_1) = \top$ |
| _(if f)_      | $< memory // if x_1 then \{label(\many{x_i'}): stmt_1\}(\many{x_i}) else stmt_2 >$ | $-->$ | $< memory // stmt_2 >$ | if $memory(x_1) = \bot$ |

_Metastack management_

|:~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~:|~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| _(new stack)_ | $< memory // x <- new stack B(\many{x_j}); stmt >$ | $-->$ | $<memory\{ x \mapsto B(\many{v_j})::\#_{marker} ::: \circ \} // stmt >$ | if $v_j = memory(x_j)$ |
| _(shift dyn)_  | $< memory // x_1 <- shift x_2; stmt >$ | $-->$ | $< memory // x_1 <- shift v; stmt >$ | if $v = memory(x_2)$ |

~ End Figblock

